Job Description
Seeking two senior-level Full Stack .NET Developers to develop and modernize enterprise applications. Candidates must have strong .NET and C# development skills, front-end/UI/UX expertise, and hands-on accessibility experience.

Key Responsibilities
Develop applications using .NET, C#, ASP.NET MVC, and Web Forms.
Build responsive interfaces using HTML5, CSS, Sass, JavaScript, Bootstrap, and Material.
Implement UI/UX best practices and enterprise design systems.
Ensure WCAG 2.1 AA and Section 508 compliance using accessibility tools such as JAWS and axe.
Develop and maintain REST APIs, middleware, and SQL Server integrations.
Manage CI/CD pipelines using Azure DevOps.
Follow secure coding practices and support production applications.

Required Skills
Strong experience with .NET, C#, and front-end development.
Proficiency in HTML5, CSS, Sass, JavaScript, and UI/UX implementation.
Formal WCAG accessibility training and hands-on accessibility testing experience.
Enterprise design system experience.
Experience with Azure DevOps, CI/CD, SQL Server, APIs, and middleware.
Experience supporting enterprise applications and handling sensitive data.
Bachelor's degree in HCI, Design, Computer Science, or a related field, or equivalent professional experience.

Preferred Qualifications
DHS Trusted Tester, IAAP WAS, or CPACC certification.
Government or healthcare project experience.
Experience with Angular, GitHub, AWS, and application modernization.
Important Submission Requirements
A code sample or portfolio demonstrating front-end and UI work is mandatory with every submission. Candidates must be available for interviews on November 3, 4, or 5, 2026.


